Online appendix for "The effects of change-decompositionon on code review - A Controlled Experiment"
submitted to the 12th International Symposium on Empirical Software Engineering 
and Measurement (ESEM '18), October 11-12, 2018, Oulu, Finland. 

Marco di Biase (m.dibiase@sig.eu), Magiel Bruntink (m.bruntink@sig.eu), 
Arie van Deursen (Arie.VanDeursen@tudelft.nl), Alberto Bacchelli (bacchelli@ifi.uzh.ch)

Source Code used in the Experiment is in folder `source_code_with_patches`.
File `jpacman.zip` contains the system; code that subject had to review is  
contained in folders `control` and `treatment` based on the group they belong
to.

Instructions provided to subjects are contained in file
`Instructions_for_the_experiment.pdf`.

Folder `Forms` contains the various forms used in the experiment.
Characterization of subjects was made using `Form_1-General_questions.pdf`.
Knowledge on the system was asked using `Form_2-Task_and_knowledge_questions.pdf`.
Review questions were asked using `Form_3-Review_questions`.

File `Other_suggested_improvements_in_reviews.xlsx` contains the comments made
by subjects that are presented in the paper as suggested improvements, and
their classification.

Replication environment is provided as a VirtualBox image, contained in folder
`virtual_machine`. Tested with VirtualBox v5.2.10.

